course: dictionary
lesson: 12984
title: Expelling: forcing out or sending away
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expelling comes from the verb expel, which means to force something out or make someone leave. The -ing ending shows the action is happening now, as in «The volcano is expelling lava.»
explain: Expelling has two main meanings. The first is about people: a school, club or country can expel someone, which means officially making them leave because of bad behaviour. Expelling a pupil is the most serious punishment, much worse than being suspended for a few days.
explain: The second meaning is about things: expelling something means pushing it out. When you breathe out, your lungs are expelling air. Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence talks about a school, a club or a country, it is about people leaving. If it talks about air, lava or gas, it means pushing something out.
fact: Expelling means forcing something out, or making someone officially leave.
fact: «Expelling a pupil» means making a pupil leave a school because of serious bad behaviour.
fact: «Expelling air» means pushing air out of your body, as when you breathe out.
fact: «Expelling» is the -ing form of expel, so it describes something happening now.
fact: Expelling a pupil is the most serious punishment: it is worse than being suspended or excluded for a few days.
exercise: «The lungs are expelling air when you breathe out.» What are the lungs doing? | Storing air for later | Pulling in air | *Pushing air out | Turning air into water
exercise: «The head teacher is expelling the pupil for fighting.» What does expelling mean here? | Giving the pupil a prize | Teaching the pupil a new game | *Making the pupil leave the school | Helping the pupil to read
exercise: «The volcano is expelling lava and ash.» What is the volcano doing? | Turning the lava into rock | Sleeping quietly | *Forcing lava and ash out | Carrying people up the hill
test: In history, rulers were «expelling» groups of people from their country. What happened to those people? | They were made into kings | They were given a new house nearby | They went on a long holiday | *They were forced to leave the country
test: Which sentence uses expelling to mean forcing something out? | The club is expelling a member for cheating. | The teacher is expelling the new pupil today. | *The engine is expelling hot gas through the pipe.
exam: Which meaning fits both «expelling air» and «expelling a pupil»? | Speaking very quietly | *Forcing something out, or making someone leave | Growing bigger and stronger | Painting a picture
